.TH OBFUSH 1 "obfush" "2.0.0-dev" "Internal tooling"
.SH NAME
obfush \- transform Bash source into an obfuscated Bash script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obfush
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page is generated from the Click command's plain \fB--help\fR output.
It documents the command surface available in this source tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: obfush [OPTIONS] [INPUT_SCRIPT] [OUTPUT_SCRIPT]

  obfush \-\- Polymorphic Bash Obfuscation Engine v2.0

  Transforms INPUT_SCRIPT into an obfuscated OUTPUT_SCRIPT. Every invocation
  produces unique output (use \-\-seed for reproducibility).

  Pre\-processing strips all source comments deterministically (shebangs
  preserved). The 11\-layer pipeline then runs in a compatibility\-DAG order;
  entropy\-mask runs last and never appends decoys after the script's tail
  statement (preserves exit codes).

  Layers (DAG\-ordered, \-\-layers selects which to enable):
    id\-mangle      Renames DEFINED vars & functions. Skips free
                   references, builtins, env\-style ALL_CAPS, and
                   PATH\-affecting commands.
    str\-shred      Hex/octal/fragment/arithmetic\-printf/base64
                   encoding of literal strings. Skips values
                   containing $\-expansions or shell syntax.
    cmd\-sub        echo<\->printf, true<\->:, source<\->., test\-style
                   morphing.
    junk\-inject    Side\-effect\-contained live dependency chains.
    flow\-obfusc    Independent\-block reordering (data\-flow aware,
                   stdout\-ordering aware), opaque predicates,
                   subshell wrapping (skips local/declare/export
                   so scope\-binding commands stay in parent shell).
    opaque\-const   Equivalent arithmetic for safe integer contexts.
    cff            Conservative straight\-line state dispatch.
    encode         Wraps commands in eval/bash\-c reconstruction chains.
                   Three modes: ok, no\-eval, direct\-exec.
    indirection    Variable & associative\-array command dispatch.
    poly\-shell     Multi\-process self\-extracting loader
                   (only at intensity >= 0.9).
    entropy\-mask   Procedural decoy injection (31,680\-combo corpus).
                   Runs LAST. Tail statement is sacred \-\- decoys
                   never appear after it.

  Quick examples:
    obfush \-\-seed 1337 in.sh out.sh           # Reproducible
    obfush \-\-batch scripts/ build/ \-\-workers 4 # Recursive batch
    obfush \-\-config .obfushrc in.sh out.sh    # YAML configuration
    obfush \-v in.sh out.sh                    # Verbose stats
    obfush \-\-eval\-mode no\-eval in.sh out.sh   # Zero eval tokens
    obfush \-\-no\-layer poly\-shell in.sh out.sh # Skip a layer
    obfush \-\-layers id\-mangle,encode \-\-min\-layers 2 in.sh out.sh
    obfush \-\-help\-advanced                    # Full doc panel

Options:
  \-\-gui                           Launch the local web dashboard.
  \-\-gui\-host TEXT                 GUI bind host.  [default: 127.0.0.1]
  \-\-gui\-port INTEGER RANGE        [default: 5000; 1<=x<=65535]
  \-\-no\-browser                    Do not open the GUI in a browser.
  \-\-setup                         Create the global ~/.obfushrc file.
  \-\-plugin FILE                   Load a trusted local layer plugin
                                  (repeatable).
  \-\-batch DIRECTORY               Process all .sh files under a directory.
  \-\-workers INTEGER RANGE         Worker processes used by batch mode.
                                  [default: 1; x>=1]
  \-\-fail\-fast                     Stop batch processing after the earliest
                                  failing input.
  \-\-config FILE                   Use an explicit YAML configuration file.
  \-\-no\-config                     Disable global and project .obfushrc
                                  discovery.
  \-\-log\-level [DEBUG|INFO|WARNING|ERROR|CRITICAL]
                                  Write structured JSON logs to stderr.
                                  [default: WARNING]
  \-\-benchmark                     Benchmark INPUT_SCRIPT without writing an
                                  output file.
  \-\-benchmark\-iterations INTEGER RANGE
                                  Measured iterations used by \-\-benchmark.
                                  [default: 5; x>=1]
  \-\-seed TEXT                     Deterministic seed (reproducible output).
  \-\-preset [stealth|standard|paranoid|godmode]
                                  Configuration profile; explicit options take
                                  precedence.
  \-\-intensity FLOAT               0.0\-1.0 obfuscation aggressiveness (default:
                                  0.8).
  \-\-layers TEXT                   Comma\-separated layers to force (overrides
                                  auto\-select).
  \-\-no\-layer TEXT                 Comma\-separated layers to disable.
  \-\-min\-layers INTEGER            Minimum active layers (default: 4).
  \-\-eval\-mode [ok|no\-eval|direct\-exec]
                                  How to handle code evaluation (default: ok).
  \-\-entropy\-target FLOAT RANGE    Target Shannon entropy (bit/byte). Default:
                                  4.5.  [0.0<=x<=8.0]
  \-\-max\-size\-ratio FLOAT RANGE    Maximum output/input byte ratio after decoy
                                  trimming.  [default: 3.0; x>=1.0]
  \-\-json\-output                   Write machine\-readable run metadata to stdout.
  \-\-output\-mode [script|binary]   Write an obfuscated shell script or Linux
                                  loader binary.  [default: script]
  \-\-env\-key TEXT                  Bind binary output to this environment key
                                  (OBFUSH_ENV_KEY may override it).
  \-\-no\-anti\-debug                 Disable best\-effort anti\-debug checks in
                                  binary output.
  \-\-checksum                      Write a SHA\-256 sidecar next to binary output
                                  for external verification.
  \-\-verify                        Run equivalence check in sandbox after emit.
  \-\-test\-input PATH               Stdin to feed both scripts during verify.
  \-v, \-\-verbose                   Show per\-layer statistics.
  \-\-dry\-run                       Print what would be done; don't write file.
  \-\-dump\-ast PATH                 Dump parsed AST to file (debug).
  \-\-help\-advanced                 Show full Spectral0x00 documentation and exit.
  \-\-version                       Show the version and exit.
  \-h, \-\-help                      Show this message and exit.

  Red Team Internal Use Only \-\- Spectral0x00
.fi
